# SRG-APP-000291-AU-000200  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must notify system administrators and ISSO when
# accounts are created.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000291-AU-000200
group:           V-221921
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000015
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk generates the notification itself: a scheduled saved search over
                 the audit records for account creation, with the email alert action
                 enabled and addressed to the system administrators and the ISSO, and an
                 SMTP relay and sender address configured in alert_actions.conf, is the
                 product's reporting and notification mechanism that the product STIG fix
                 text directs an administrator to use.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] from matches ^[^@[:space:]]+@[^@[:space:]]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] action.email in 1|true
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] action.email.to non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] from non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] from matches ^[^@[:space:]]+@[^@[:space:]]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] from https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The SMTP relay that accepts and delivers the message is a separate
                 component; the product specification states plainly that a mail server "is
                 not included with the Splunk instance".
external:        Which addresses belong to the system administrators and the ISSO is
                 organization-defined, as is the reporting frequency expressed in the cron
                 schedule; the criterion tests that recipients and a schedule are
                 expressed, not their values.
external:        The product STIG verifies this by interviewing the administrator that a
                 report exists and the ISSO that it is received, so confirmation of receipt
                 is a procedural step outside the application.
external:        Whether the saved search's own query selects account-creation records is a
                 matter of search language content rather than a configuration value, and
                 needs reviewer inspection alongside these conditions.
external:        Account creations performed in an external directory service or identity
                 provider are notified from the records that component sends to Splunk, so
                 coverage depends on those sources being onboarded.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/alert_actions.conf.spec:157-166 ([email], from =
                 <string>, default splunk), 276-285 (mailserver = <host>[:<port>], SMTP
                 server "is not included with the Splunk instance", default localhost);
                 splunk-spec-files/savedsearches.conf.spec:73-78 (enableSched = [0 | 1],
                 default 0), 79-90 (cron_schedule), 249-254 (counttype), 270-274
                 (alert_condition), 300-303 (action.email = <boolean>, default false),
                 304-307 (action.email.to = <email list>, REQUIRED, empty default); product
                 STIG SPLK-CL-000020 check and fix text.
finding:         Splunk is not configured to notify the system administrators and the ISSO
                 when accounts are created, because no scheduled saved search with the
                 email action enabled and addressed to those recipients exists, or
                 alert_actions.conf [email] names no SMTP relay or sender for the
                 notification to be sent through; this is assessed at the application layer
                 alone, with the mail relay, the recipient addresses, the notification
                 frequency, and the ISSO's confirmation of receipt recorded as external
                 dependencies.
